  "verbalization": "Dragmacidin E is implicated in the target pathway leading to PITSLRE serine/threonine-protein kinase CDC2L1 through multiple indirect routes. The first pathway links Dragmacidin E to Lumican, which is targeted by levamisole, and levamisole further targets CDC2L1. This suggests a potential regulatory chain where Dragmacidin E influences Lumican, which in turn is affected by levamisole, ultimately affecting CDC2L1. The second and third pathways reveal that Dragmacidin E also targets a sodium/bile acid cotransporter, which is subsequently targeted by two different compounds, both of which also target CDC2L1. These findings collectively indicate that Dragmacidin E may act as a modulator of the CDC2L1 kinase through various molecular interactions, possibly by influencing the activity or expression of the sodium/bile acid cotransporter or other downstream targets. The integration of these pathways highlights the complex, multi-tiered mechanism by which Dragmacidin E could influence the function of PITSLRE serine/threonine-protein kinase CDC2L1, emphasizing the importance of understanding the broader biological context in which these interactions occur.",
